# Agent Test Cleanup (Files + Database)

**Default:** Agents must not leave behind **test files** or **test database rows** unless the user explicitly asks to keep them.

This overrides TDD / "add tests before done" guidance when the user has not requested tests.

## Test SKU patterns (never persist)

| Pattern | Examples |
| --- | --- |
| `E2E-*` | `E2E-RESTOCK-1787033168675`, `E2E-PO-*`, `E2E-BETA-*` |
| `ARCH-UI-*`, `BR-UI-*` | Archive/UI QA fixtures |
| `*UI-TEST*` in SKU | Ad-hoc UI test products |
| Description contains | `UI TEST KIT`, `E2E Restock`, `E2E Product`, `E2E PO Product`, `E2E Manual Upload` |

Shared guard: `App\Support\Products\AgentTestSkuGuard`.

## Before handoff (mandatory)

### 1. Test files

- **Delete** any new test files (`tests/**`, `**/*.spec.ts`, `resources/js/**/__tests__/**`).
- **Revert** edits to existing test files (`git checkout -- <path>`).
- Confirm `git status` shows no unsolicited test paths.

### 2. Test database rows

If you created products, PO lines, taxonomy verifications, Plamod rows, or any ERP record for QA:

- **Delete them** before marking the task done.
- Purge script (local Docker): `docker exec -i pricing-tool-mysql mysql -uroot -proot pricing_tool < scripts/purge-agent-test-skus.sql`
- Verify zero rows: `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM products WHERE sku LIKE 'E2E-%';` must be **0** after your session unless the user asked to keep fixtures.

### 3. Do not pollute operator UIs

- Never run bulk taxonomy research/approve against ad-hoc `E2E-*` products you created for browser QA.
- Taxonomy review **excludes** agent test SKUs via `AgentTestSkuGuard` — do not bypass this.

## Allowed verification (without leaving debris)

- Real browser / manual API on **existing real SKUs** when possible.
- Temporary `E2E-*` rows only for in-session debugging — **purge before handoff**.
- Run existing project tests when useful; do not add new spec files.

## Exceptions

- User explicitly asks for tests or permanent fixtures.
- User opens a PR and requests test coverage.
- Minimal fix to an **existing** broken test the user owns.

## Forbidden handoffs

- `E2E-*` / `E2E-RESTOCK-*` rows visible on Products or Taxonomy review (screenshot-able proof of failure).
- New or modified test files "for later".
- Saying "tests pass" while test SKUs remain in the database.
